   "text": "For months they hammer the walls, and the walls hold. But the Persians don't give up, and they don't go home. So the smith starts walking the inside of the wall. He sets his shield down, kneels, listens, then moves a few steps and does it again. \"Lost something?\" a guard laughs. \"The enemy's out there, not down there.\"",
